# Check prior specs before re-fixing

If the bug is on a surface we already specced or shipped in this repo, **read those specs first**. Do not invent a second layout or search rule that fights the first.

```
openspec/changes/<change>/specs/**/spec.md
openspec/specs/**/spec.md   (after archive)
```

## Do

- Search `openspec/changes/` and `openspec/specs/` for the capability (Now Singing cards, Scripture grid, song live-sync, shortcuts, …).
- Keep the existing WHEN/THEN true. A new fix is a delta, not a rewrite.
- If two specs conflict, stop and say so — do not silently pick.

## Do not

```
// ❌ BAD — Scripture already specs “3 columns fill width, hug height”
//          then a later fix switches to ragged WrapPanel widths
//          because the width binding failed.

// ✅ GOOD — same spec; bind width on the card item (Now Singing pattern)
//          so columns still fill and cards stay short
```

Tiny typos/comments can skip this. New workstreams still go explore → spec → TDD.
